{
  "@context": "https://linkedsoftwaredependencies.org/bundles/npm/@solid/community-server/^7.0.0/components/context.jsonld",
  "import": [
    "css:config/app/init/initialize-intro.json",
    "css:config/app/main/default.json",
    "css:config/app/variables/default.json",
    "css:config/http/handler/default.json",
    "css:config/http/middleware/default.json",
    "css:config/http/notifications/all.json",
    "css:config/http/server-factory/http.json",
    "css:config/http/static/default.json",
    "css:config/identity/access/public.json",
    "css:config/identity/email/default.json",
    "css:config/identity/handler/default.json",
    "css:config/identity/oidc/default.json",
    "css:config/identity/ownership/token.json",
    "css:config/identity/pod/static.json",
    "css:config/ldp/authorization/webacl.json",
    "css:config/ldp/handler/default.json",
    "css:config/ldp/metadata-parser/default.json",
    "css:config/ldp/metadata-writer/default.json",
    "css:config/ldp/modes/default.json",
    "css:config/storage/backend/file.json",
    "css:config/storage/key-value/resource-store.json",
    "css:config/storage/location/root.json",
    "css:config/storage/middleware/default.json",
    "css:config/util/auxiliary/acl.json",
    "css:config/util/identifiers/suffix.json",
    "css:config/util/index/default.json",
    "css:config/util/logging/winston.json",
    "css:config/util/representation-conversion/default.json",
    "css:config/util/resource-locker/memory.json",
    "css:config/util/variables/default.json"
  ],
  "@graph": [
    {
      "comment": [
        "PoC dev config: file-system storage.",
        "Story 7.1: custom CredentialsExtractor unions the REAL Solid-OIDC token path",
        "(DPoP + Bearer, from css:config/ldp/authentication/dpop-bearer.json) WITH the",
        "debug UnsecureWebIdExtractor (Authorization: WebID <uri>, from debug-auth-header.json).",
        "Both auth base configs define urn:solid-server:default:CredentialsExtractor, so they",
        "cannot both be imported; this restates the combined waterfall in one definition instead.",
        "Why both are needed: real backoffice users (Epic 7) authenticate via OIDC and were getting",
        "a blanket 401 on every write/.acl request because debug-auth-header alone dropped the DPoP",
        "extractor entirely. The ~15 internal automation files (pipeline/, agents/) still rely on the",
        "WebID header via the Docker-internal CSS_CONNECT_URL path.",
        "SECURITY: UnsecureWebIdExtractor trusts Authorization: WebID <uri> with no verification.",
        "That header is stripped at the nginx-gateway edge for all public traffic (Story 4.4.1,",
        "04-pocpod0.conf), so it is only reachable from inside the Docker network. DO NOT remove",
        "that edge stripping. DO NOT USE this debug extractor on a server exposed without it."
      ],
      "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:CredentialsExtractor",
      "@type": "CachedHandler",
      "source": {
        "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:UnionCredentialsExtractor",
        "@type": "UnionCredentialsExtractor",
        "extractors": [
          {
            "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:AccessTokenExtractor",
            "@type": "WaterfallHandler",
            "handlers": [
              {
                "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:DPoPWebIdExtractor",
                "@type": "DPoPWebIdExtractor",
                "originalUrlExtractor": {
                  "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:DPoPUrlExtractor",
                  "@type": "OriginalUrlExtractor",
                  "args_identifierStrategy": { "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:IdentifierStrategy" }
                }
              },
              {
                "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:BearerWebIdExtractor",
                "@type": "BearerWebIdExtractor"
              }
            ]
          },
          { "@type": "UnsecureWebIdExtractor" },
          {
            "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:PublicCredentialsExtractor",
            "@type": "PublicCredentialsExtractor"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": [
        "Story 7.1: serve the pod backoffice at the root of pod.nicolasdb.eu instead of the CSS",
        "default welcome page. Additive to css:config/http/static/default.json's",
        "StaticAssetHandler (same @id) - Components.js concatenates the array-valued `assets`",
        "property across definitions sharing an @id, so only new entries are listed here;",
        "redeclaring @type/baseUrl/options_expires here would conflict with the base definition."
      ],
      "@id": "urn:solid-server:default:StaticAssetHandler",
      "@type": "StaticAssetHandler",
      "assets": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:solid-server:pocpod0:BackofficeIndexAsset",
          "@type": "StaticAssetEntry",
          "relativeUrl": "/",
          "filePath": "/backoffice/index.html"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:solid-server:pocpod0:BackofficePodApiAsset",
          "@type": "StaticAssetEntry",
          "relativeUrl": "/pod-api.js",
          "filePath": "/backoffice/pod-api.js"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:solid-server:pocpod0:BackofficeSupportAsset",
          "@type": "StaticAssetEntry",
          "relativeUrl": "/support.js",
          "filePath": "/backoffice/support.js"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:solid-server:pocpod0:DesignTokensAsset",
          "@type": "StaticAssetEntry",
          "relativeUrl": "/tokens.css",
          "filePath": "/backoffice/tokens.css"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
